Z||000000||zeusrekning||06-22-2000||11:03 PM||||OK. If i lift my car up so no wheels are touching the ground i can move my rear drivers side wheel back and forth( holding it at th3 3 o'clock and 9 o'clock position). <BR>I know the problem is the toe link rod. You can see the rod moving where it goes into the boot that is bolted to the cradle. Some one told me that they thin this can be tightened. there is about 1 inch total movement 1/2 inch both ways. <P>And, with the car on the ground i was checking each wheel. I noticed movement in the front drivers side wheel. the passengers side had no movement. so i jacked the fds of the car up with the wheel on you can make it move mabey a 1/4" both ways mabey a little less. with the wheel of holding the brake rotor it isn't as bad. The wheel was on good and tight. it felt like it was moving at the bottom of the spindle. Sorry so vague but not sure about the front suspension.<BR>Thanks for any help. My suspension is bad. It is like driving a boat, you hit something uneven and you sway.<P>Ps about 4 months ago i had an accident and I went of the interstate into a gully doing about 60. niether me or the car were hurt. a briar bush stopped me. I'm not sure if my suspension caused the wreck or if the wreck messed up my suspinsion.<BR>I'm afraid it may happen again.<BR>Oh, I have an 87 coupe 4cyl 5 speed. will a toe link rod off of any 4cyl fiero work. If not which years? ||||reg||4
Z||000001||2FAST4U||06-22-2000||11:57 PM||||Better get that toe link fixwd soon or other parts will start to break - besides being dangrous and hard to drive. All 84-87 toe rods are the same. I just bought new ones for my car ( about 75.00 each from GM) I've got two good used ones I'll give you for the price of shipping.<P>As for the problem on the front - side to side movement with hands at 3:00 and 9:00 is usually a bad tie rod end. top to bottom or in and out movement with hands at the 6:00 and 12:00 is usually a bad ball joint.<P>Hope this helps.<P>JOE<BR>(2FAST4U)<p>[This message has been edited by 2FAST4U (edited 06-22-2000).]||||reg||1
